# Commit on land

When a phase artifact, handoff, founder lock, or other company file **lands on disk**, commit those paths and push to `origin` (`https://github.com/makemoney2023/SourceControl.git`) in the same turn. Do not wait for the operator to ask.

## Scope

- Stage **only** the files that just landed (and this rule, if you edited it). Do not sweep unrelated dirty trees (Blacksage, graphify, income-stack, lemonade-stand, memorybank apikeys).
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, tokens, or `**/apikeys/**`.
- Do not `git add -A`.
- Do not change git config (`user.name` / `user.email` stay as-is).

## Commit

Working tree: `/Users/cbsuperpatch/Desktop/ClaudeSkills` (branch `main`).

Message style matches the log: `feat(telltail): …` / `docs(org): …` — one sentence on why.

```
git add <landed-paths>
git commit -m "feat(telltail): <what landed>"
```

## Push

`git push origin main`.

This Mac’s `gh` often has **SuperPatchAi** active. SourceControl write access is **makemoney2023**. If push returns Permission denied to SuperPatchAi / 403:

1. `gh auth switch --user makemoney2023`
2. `git push origin main`
3. `gh auth switch --user SuperPatchAi` (leave their default account as it was)

Do not paste tokens. Do not force-push.

## Orchestrator note

C-suite approve + runbook mark counts as a land. Commit the new/changed files under `docs/projects/<venture>/` (and the tracker) then push before opening the next phase.
